course: dictionary
lesson: 1477
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» The words life cycle and butterfly show that caterpillar is a stage in a butterfly's life, a long, soft creature.
explain: «The hairs of some caterpillars, such as the oak processionary, cause rashes, so you do not touch hairy caterpillars.» The clues are hairs, rashes and do not touch, so caterpillar means the living creature itself.
explain: Now look at «a caterpillar track». A Caterpillar track is a moving metal belt around the wheels of a tractor or tank. The clues are metal and wheels, not an animal. Always ask: does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: A caterpillar is the long, soft, worm-like larva of a butterfly or moth, with many legs.
fact: In a butterfly's life cycle, the caterpillar comes after the egg and before the chrysalis.
fact: Caterpillars eat leaves and grow quickly, shedding their skin several times.
fact: Some caterpillars have hairs that sting or cause itchy rashes, so look but do not touch.
fact: A Caterpillar track is a moving metal belt around the wheels of a tractor or tank.
exercise: «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» Which stage comes straight after the egg? | Chrysalis | Butterfly | *Caterpillar | Frog
exercise: What is a Caterpillar track? | A type of butterfly | A tiny insect with a hairy body | *A moving metal belt around the wheels of a tractor or tank | A leaf-eating larva
exercise: Why should you look at hairy caterpillars but not touch them? | *Because some have hairs that sting or cause itchy rashes | Because they are made of metal | Because they are very sweet | Because they are too big to lift
test: «Many animals change shape completely as they grow up: a tadpole becomes a frog, a caterpillar becomes a butterfly.» In this sentence, what does the caterpillar become? | *Butterfly | Chrysalis | Frog | Tadpole
test: Which sentence uses caterpillar to mean a machine part? | The caterpillar hid under the leaf | *The tractor's caterpillar tracks gripped the muddy field | The caterpillar ate a whole leaf in a day | The caterpillar shed its skin
exam: In «a large blue caterpillar "with its arms folded, quietly smoking a long hookah"», which clue shows the caterpillar is a living creature? | Metal belt | Big mushroom | Tractor wheels | *Arms folded and smoking a hookah
